      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Percutaneous interventional spinal procedures have become ubiquitous in the management of cervical pain syndromes. This article reviews the indications, contraindications, patient selection, and potential complications of epidural injections, zygapophyseal joint and medial branch nerve injections, spinal cord stimulation, and radiofrequency neurotomy."
